    "title": "Crestwood man charged after fumes sicken 8 first responders - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alonzo Small ,\n7 hours ago\nCRESTWOOD, Ill. ( WGN ) — A Crestwood man faces drug charges after more than a dozen first responders became ill while responding to a well-being check.\nCalled to the 12700 block of S. Central Ave., emergency crews found a man, later identified as John Fiacchino, unresponsive inside the apartment.\nCrestwood police said the Sept. 30 incident resulted in eight responders – four firefighters and four police officers – receiving treatment at a local hospital after “experiencing negative effects from fumes.”\nAll were later released, but the incident prompted a HAZMAT team response.\nSEE ALSO | Puppy scams surge during holidays with popular breeds targeted, BBB warns Detectives shipped substances collected inside the apartment to the Illinois State Police Crime Lab for analysis.\nUpon review, authorities arrested Fiacchino on Tuesday. Cook County prosecutors charged him with possession with the intent to deliver methamphetamine and possession with the intent to deliver psilocybin (mushrooms), both of which are felonies.\nFiacchino also faces a reckless conduct charge.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WGN-TV.",
